From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dwrite: a glyph's bitmap is cached per rendering mode

A glyph's aliased bitmap (1 bit a pixel, its own pitch) and its smoothed one shared one cache entry; the mode that drew the glyph second read the first one's bitmap with its own pitch, every other row of the glyph lost. Chromium draws a font both ways (Tahoma's bitmap strikes in Cursor and VS Code).
---
diff --git a/dlls/dwrite/font.c b/dlls/dwrite/font.c
index d628f53..8e871df 100644
--- a/dlls/dwrite/font.c
+++ b/dlls/dwrite/font.c
@@ -242,6 +242,15 @@ static HRESULT dwrite_fontface_get_glyph_bitmap(struct dwrite_fontface *fontface
     params.is_1bpp = is_1bpp;
     params.offset_x = key.offset_x = bitmap->offset_x;
     params.offset_y = key.offset_y = bitmap->offset_y;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DW_BITMAP_ONE_ENTRY
+    /* Stained Glass OS: a glyph's aliased bitmap (1 bit a pixel, its own
+       pitch) and its smoothed one were one cache entry: whichever mode drew
+       the glyph first, the other read that bitmap back with its own pitch --
+       every other row of the glyph dropped, or a 1bpp glyph read as gray.
+       Bitmaps are kept per rendering mode, apart from the advances' entries
+       of a measuring mode. */
+    key.mode = 0x100 | rendering_mode;
+#endif
     matrix_2x2_from_dwrite_matrix(&params.m, bitmap->m ? bitmap->m : &identity);
     fold_transform_scale(&params.emsize, &params.m);
     key.size = params.emsize;
